stateDiagram-v2
  state ComparisonWorkspace {
    state Screen {
      [*] --> Visible
      Visible --> Cached: Close panel or switch subject
      Cached --> Visible: Reopen this subject
      Visible --> Retired: Access retired
      Cached --> Retired: Access retired
      Retired --> Visible: Remount after authorized detail retry
    }
    --
    state Comparison {
      [*] --> Mounted
      state Mounted {
        [*] --> Loading
        Loading --> History: Valid response with focus off
        Loading --> Focused: Valid response with focus on
        Loading --> Error: Failed or malformed response
        History --> Focused: Check Hide superseded terms
        Focused --> History: Clear Hide superseded terms
        History --> History: Change term, stage, or expense basis
        Focused --> Focused: Change term, stage, or expense basis
        History --> Loading: Compare again
        Focused --> Loading: Compare again
        Error --> Loading: Retry Compare
      }
      Mounted --> Disposed: Access retired
      Disposed --> Mounted: Remount after authorized detail retry
    }
  }
  %% never RetiredMounted: Retired & Mounted -- Retired access never displays or accepts late comparison results.
  %% never VisibleDisposed: Visible & Disposed -- An authorized remount starts a fresh comparison.
  %% Screen describes this subject; switching subjects caches its mounted comparison and opens the other subject's independent view.
  %% Closing changes only Screen. Responses may settle while cached. Reopening reattaches the existing comparison without a read or focus reset.
  %% Access retirement disposes every cached subject. Explicit component disposal/remount has the same fresh-focus semantics.
  %% Focus survives Compare, empty and malformed responses; History and Focused describe successful results, including an empty result.
  %% Projection rules checked by the browser matrix: never hide without a matching successor in the complete response; local controls preserve coverage and make no read.
  %% System design: Comparison owns the boolean and validated response; Results owns the local projection.
  %% The workspace owns a session-scoped per-subject mount cache, cleared on actor change or access refusal (js/pipeline.js:343,870,1099).
  %% Use one successor predicate for styling and visibility. Keep the mount interface unchanged except an additive parser export for proof admission.
  %% Capacity: existing rows.some is quadratic; reuse its result once per row before filtering. At 10x the response, rendering and this scan grow first. No new infrastructure.
  %% Load spread, storage, N+1 and persistent cache: n/a, one existing read and no new storage access. Successful reads replace the response.
  %% Consistency: project only the latest validated response. Malformed and failed reads refuse; stale reads cannot replace the latest view.
  %% Async: existing Compare sequence guards responses. No queue, new calls, fan-out, retries, circuit breaker, rate limit, write or idempotency key is added.
  %% External failures use existing explicit retry behavior. Local controls make zero requests.
  %% Throughput checkpoint: reproduce the chart contradiction, cover real workspace entry points, then serial focused and full verification.
